WEBVTT

00:04.713 --> 00:05.797
I can win!

00:06.339 --> 00:07.590
Against Reiner...

00:08.216 --> 00:09.175
I can win!

00:15.932 --> 00:16.808
Hey...

00:16.891 --> 00:18.226
Hey!

00:18.893 --> 00:21.604
Above you! Look out!

01:41.893 --> 01:44.437
Eren!

03:31.377 --> 03:34.756
TROST DISTRICT

03:43.389 --> 03:44.432
Commander.

03:45.683 --> 03:47.936
Wake up, Commander Pyxis.

03:49.354 --> 03:51.356
You'll get sick if you fall asleep here.

03:52.941 --> 03:54.817
I can't believe you drank all this.

03:55.652 --> 03:57.153
You're not young anymore.

03:58.071 --> 04:01.241
And I'd rather not spend my days
changing your diapers.

04:01.991 --> 04:05.495
I don't mind being cared for
by a pretty lady.

04:06.079 --> 04:07.497
Well? What's the situation?

04:09.707 --> 04:11.668
Once the Titans were gone,
patrols were sent out

04:11.960 --> 04:15.004
from the first and second defensive lines.

04:15.630 --> 04:18.633
But Titan sightings
are few and far between.

04:20.301 --> 04:24.180
If Hannes and the advance squad
followed the wall without a problem,

04:24.430 --> 04:26.599
they should be returning any minute now.

04:28.142 --> 04:31.938
It would mean they met with the unit
from Krolva District

04:32.021 --> 04:34.232
and turned around halfway.

04:35.942 --> 04:39.362
They couldn't have encountered
many Titans.

04:40.238 --> 04:44.492
If there was a hole in the wall,
it would never work out like that.

04:48.288 --> 04:49.330
Commander Pyxis.

04:51.499 --> 04:53.251
Oh, Erwin, it's you.

04:54.877 --> 04:58.256
I hear you've captured
one of those troublesome mice.

04:58.464 --> 04:59.382
Yes.

04:59.674 --> 05:02.218
Unfortunately, we were one step behind.

05:04.554 --> 05:07.807
But at least it will get those goons
in the interior thinking.

05:08.433 --> 05:13.354
Maybe they'll reconsider how important
their stale beliefs and motives are.

05:14.022 --> 05:16.149
Yes, it appears they will.

05:16.941 --> 05:18.109
Look over there.

05:18.693 --> 05:23.948
The Military Police have finally been
forced to be in an area that has Titans.

05:26.159 --> 05:29.037
I can't believe we didn't see any Titans.

05:29.579 --> 05:30.913
Were there really none at all?

05:31.456 --> 05:34.250
It seems so.
It's unusually quiet out there.

05:38.504 --> 05:40.173
I wonder if they're still alive.

05:40.798 --> 05:43.843
Can you believe it?
I thought this was an emergency.

05:44.010 --> 05:46.637
Yes. But everyone here
is just sitting around.

05:47.305 --> 05:48.347
Hey, Levi.

05:48.681 --> 05:50.516
Where have you hidden the Titans?

05:51.934 --> 05:55.229
What? You all seem so disappointed.

05:56.731 --> 06:00.026
Sorry. It's a shame
you couldn't fight Titans today.

06:00.818 --> 06:03.446
If you want another chance,

06:04.072 --> 06:06.282
there are plenty of expeditions
outside the walls.

06:07.533 --> 06:10.912
How about we join forces
and face some Titans together?

06:12.830 --> 06:14.123
Well, you know...

06:14.373 --> 06:16.250
We're busy with work in the interior.

06:16.793 --> 06:18.461
The advance squad has returned!

06:19.212 --> 06:20.630
Inform Commander Pyxis!

06:24.675 --> 06:25.593
I see.

06:26.260 --> 06:28.679
So there was nothing wrong with the wall?

06:29.347 --> 06:30.306
None, sir!

06:31.724 --> 06:32.850
As I had suspected.

06:35.895 --> 06:38.981
However, there's a bit of a situation!

06:39.607 --> 06:42.485
We were heading back to Trost
to give our report

06:42.735 --> 06:45.571
when we ran into the Scout unit
led by Section Commander Hanji.

06:45.947 --> 06:50.368
Along with them, there were recruits
from the 104th without their equipment.

06:50.868 --> 06:52.453
And it turns out that three of them...

06:53.579 --> 06:54.747
They were Titans!

06:57.166 --> 06:58.835
What are you talking about?

06:59.335 --> 07:01.212
Are you saying there were more?

07:02.130 --> 07:03.589
Three more of them?

07:04.257 --> 07:05.174
Who were they?

07:06.384 --> 07:07.301
Well...

07:07.552 --> 07:08.719
Relax, Jean.

07:10.221 --> 07:12.140
What happened
when their forms were revealed?

07:12.890 --> 07:16.519
The Scouts engaged the Colossal Titan
and the Armored Titan in battle.

07:18.146 --> 07:20.398
But by the time we joined the fight,

07:20.857 --> 07:23.151
it was all over.

07:42.336 --> 07:45.131
Unbelievable! What a disaster!

07:46.090 --> 07:48.759
Luckily, we were up here,
so we got away unscathed.

07:49.760 --> 07:52.221
Everyone underneath got affected
by the steam and wind.

07:52.388 --> 07:54.056
There's nothing they could have done.

07:57.685 --> 07:58.769
How's Mikasa doing?

07:59.520 --> 08:01.481
I don't see a life-threatening wound.

08:01.981 --> 08:03.566
I'm guessing it's just a concussion.

08:04.442 --> 08:05.568
I see...

08:07.737 --> 08:10.281
Armin, you haven't eaten, have you?

08:10.990 --> 08:12.116
I'll get you something to eat.

08:15.995 --> 08:17.079
You have to eat.

08:31.010 --> 08:31.969
Mikasa!

08:35.723 --> 08:37.475
Mikasa! It's Eren!

08:38.476 --> 08:39.477
What happened to Eren?

08:41.020 --> 08:42.438
It's those three bullies again.

08:42.813 --> 08:44.690
They took some bread I bought for myself,

08:45.107 --> 08:47.401
so he went on his own to get--

08:48.569 --> 08:49.695
I tried to stop him!

08:51.989 --> 08:52.990
Wait!

08:54.367 --> 08:55.451
Give it back!

08:56.160 --> 09:00.081
I thought I told you already.
There's none left because I ate it.

09:00.456 --> 09:01.290
Got it?

09:01.415 --> 09:03.876
That was three days' worth of food
for his family!

09:04.168 --> 09:06.420
You've got to be kidding me.
Those table scraps?

09:07.672 --> 09:09.757
Quit it, man. I feel bad now.

09:10.341 --> 09:12.802
If you're fine with it coming out
as vomit, I'll give it back.

09:16.597 --> 09:19.016
Pay him back for what you took!

09:24.689 --> 09:25.815
Hey! Knock it off!

09:26.148 --> 09:26.983
Hey!

09:27.149 --> 09:29.443
You drunk, good-for-nothing soldiers!

09:29.735 --> 09:31.279
Come and break up this fight!

09:31.362 --> 09:32.989
Put a sock in it.

09:33.406 --> 09:35.825
Can't you see
the kids are just fooling around?

09:36.075 --> 09:38.578
Like hell they're fooling around!
Come and stop them!

09:40.913 --> 09:43.291
It will be fine, I'm telling you.

09:43.416 --> 09:46.335
Someone who can help you more than us
will come along.

09:46.877 --> 09:47.920
What?

09:50.548 --> 09:51.549
Eren!

09:52.592 --> 09:53.593
Take this!

10:03.311 --> 10:04.228
It's Mikasa--

10:05.563 --> 10:08.024
Mikasa! Why are you here?

10:08.399 --> 10:12.653
Eren, if you don't get home and cut wood,
your mother will get angry again.

10:13.362 --> 10:15.865
You wretch! Don't underestimate me!

10:17.450 --> 10:18.492
You asked for it--

10:18.951 --> 10:19.827
Eren!

10:20.036 --> 10:21.245
Let Mikasa handle this!

10:21.454 --> 10:22.538
As if!

10:26.042 --> 10:27.335
Nice one, Eren!

10:27.460 --> 10:29.170
Don't lose to Mikasa!

10:31.756 --> 10:32.965
What the hell are you doing?

10:33.049 --> 10:35.843
I told you to stop the fight,
you damn freeloaders!

10:36.177 --> 10:37.261
What was that?

10:38.054 --> 10:39.597
You want to say that again?

10:39.680 --> 10:42.600
Damn right, I do! You're a waste of taxes!

10:42.892 --> 10:43.976
You son of a--

10:44.060 --> 10:45.269
Don't let it get to you.

10:45.394 --> 10:47.146
It's the truth whether you like it or--

10:52.985 --> 10:56.906
That was a pretty good punch
for a chump who runs a stall.

11:07.166 --> 11:09.585
Get him! Knock his lights out, Hannes!

11:10.002 --> 11:12.505
You've got this!
Don't let that useless turd beat you!

11:13.422 --> 11:14.548
Hey, you idiots!

11:14.965 --> 11:16.300
What the hell are you doing?

11:16.967 --> 11:18.636
-Cut it out!
-Give it back!

11:24.809 --> 11:25.976
Damn it!

11:29.897 --> 11:31.023
Knock it off!

11:32.066 --> 11:35.694
Hey! This is getting pretty serious!

11:37.321 --> 11:38.864
Forget it! Let's scram!

11:38.989 --> 11:39.990
Wait right there!

11:42.284 --> 11:43.244
Wait!

11:43.327 --> 11:47.081
Eren! I don't care about
the bread anymore! Thanks for trying!

11:47.623 --> 11:49.834
Eren, we should also head home.

11:50.251 --> 11:51.585
Go home without me!

11:51.669 --> 11:52.545
Eren!

11:52.628 --> 11:53.671
Stop right there!

11:54.547 --> 11:56.257
Eren! Wait!

12:00.010 --> 12:01.720
Eren!

12:23.075 --> 12:23.951
Mikasa?

12:25.077 --> 12:26.537
Armin! Where's Eren?

12:26.912 --> 12:28.122
Mikasa, calm down--

12:28.873 --> 12:30.082
You shouldn't be moving!

12:30.332 --> 12:32.209
We don't know how badly you're injured!

12:43.012 --> 12:44.096
Where is he?

12:45.473 --> 12:46.974
Eren was taken away.

12:49.435 --> 12:51.854
And so was Ymir. By Bertholdt and Reiner.

12:55.983 --> 12:57.151
Eren, he...

12:58.152 --> 13:00.112
He lost to the Armored Titan.

13:02.114 --> 13:04.158
It's been five hours since then.

13:06.619 --> 13:07.703
Is anyone...

13:08.746 --> 13:10.289
Is anyone going after them?

13:15.169 --> 13:16.128
No.

13:16.212 --> 13:17.129
Why not?

13:20.049 --> 13:22.843
All the horses are on the other side
of the wall.

13:26.555 --> 13:27.890
In order to rescue Eren,

13:28.474 --> 13:31.977
we have to wait for lifts to come,
so we can move the horses.

13:32.561 --> 13:34.104
There's nothing we can do.

13:35.648 --> 13:37.983
Section Commander Hanji
and the other officers

13:38.067 --> 13:39.401
are too injured to move.

13:40.194 --> 13:42.446
To even send out a small scouting party,

13:42.696 --> 13:44.865
we're going to need
more soldiers than this.

13:45.991 --> 13:47.117
Soldiers with experience.

13:48.702 --> 13:49.745
Understand?

13:58.254 --> 13:59.421
Not again.

14:00.214 --> 14:01.423
Are you in pain?

14:02.424 --> 14:03.300
No...

14:03.842 --> 14:05.886
I must have hit my head pretty hard,

14:06.387 --> 14:07.388
but I'm fine.

14:08.097 --> 14:09.139
But...

14:10.057 --> 14:11.767
When Eren was taken away by Annie,

14:13.394 --> 14:14.853
I chased them right away.

14:15.688 --> 14:18.941
And in the end,
by fighting alongside Captain Levi,

14:20.484 --> 14:23.028
we were able to get him back.

14:27.575 --> 14:30.536
But now, it's already been five hours.

14:43.340 --> 14:45.092
Hey, Armin.

14:46.510 --> 14:47.511
Why?

14:48.554 --> 14:51.891
Why does Eren always go
somewhere far from us?

14:53.809 --> 14:56.061
Right, now that you mention it...

14:57.104 --> 15:00.608
Eren has always run off on his own,

15:01.066 --> 15:02.276
leaving us behind.

15:04.236 --> 15:07.907
I guess that's just
how things are meant to happen.

15:08.741 --> 15:10.034
For Eren, at least.

15:17.374 --> 15:18.459
But all I want

15:19.126 --> 15:20.753
is to be by his side.

15:27.009 --> 15:28.302
That's all I ask for.

15:40.814 --> 15:42.691
Mikasa? You're up?

15:44.401 --> 15:45.486
I bet you're hungry.

15:45.903 --> 15:46.946
Here, eat this.

15:48.739 --> 15:49.823
Catch, Armin.

15:52.201 --> 15:55.579
As usual, field rations are all there is.

16:01.543 --> 16:04.964
Tastes neither good nor bad.
Same as always.

16:10.928 --> 16:13.472
Speaking of which,
this situation is quite familiar too.

16:14.098 --> 16:17.059
You two have been there
to clean up that brat's mess

16:17.142 --> 16:19.019
ever since the good old days.

16:20.437 --> 16:23.440
That's what I call
a lousy relationship. Jeez.

16:24.483 --> 16:27.444
It's a different time
and a different place,

16:27.653 --> 16:30.656
but you kids are doing the same thing
you always have.

16:31.573 --> 16:32.700
Am I right?

16:34.493 --> 16:36.787
The neighborhood bullies are
a little different from the Titans

16:37.204 --> 16:39.123
when it comes to size.

16:39.999 --> 16:45.129
True. The thing is,
that brat isn't all that good at fighting.

16:45.462 --> 16:50.175
Whether he's up against three or five
of them, he'd charge in all the same.

16:50.634 --> 16:54.930
By the time soldiers or Mikasa showed up,
he'd been beaten to a pulp.

16:56.974 --> 16:57.975
But you know...

16:59.893 --> 17:02.479
I've never seen him win a fight before,

17:02.730 --> 17:05.691
but I've never seen him get beaten up
and give up either.

17:09.403 --> 17:13.866
Sometimes he's so tenacious
that even I think it's scary.

17:14.742 --> 17:17.786
No matter how many times
he's knocked over, he gets back up.

17:18.454 --> 17:19.621
That's the kind of guy he is.

17:20.122 --> 17:23.000
You think he'll get taken away
without putting up a fight?

17:24.168 --> 17:27.629
No way. He'll keep resisting
as long as he has the strength.

17:28.297 --> 17:30.632
Even more so
when he's up against just two opponents.

17:31.383 --> 17:34.344
No matter who he's up against,
he'll give them a tough time.

17:34.845 --> 17:36.972
Until you or I show up to help.

17:37.473 --> 17:39.266
That's how Eren has always been.

17:47.232 --> 17:49.943
I loved those good old days.

17:51.195 --> 17:52.362
If you ask Eren,

17:52.988 --> 17:56.450
he'd say that the peace during those days
was nothing but a sham.

17:57.826 --> 18:02.581
But for me, I'm more than happy
to be a drunk, useless soldier.

18:04.333 --> 18:07.753
To get those plain, ordinary days back,

18:08.170 --> 18:09.922
I will do whatever it takes.

18:11.215 --> 18:13.592
No matter how long it takes
to bring it back.

18:15.302 --> 18:16.512
I'll come along.

18:17.346 --> 18:22.017
Without the three of you together again,
I can't bring back the good old days.

18:52.422 --> 18:53.465
They're here!

18:54.299 --> 18:55.217
Hey!

18:55.551 --> 18:56.635
Isn't that...

18:59.221 --> 19:00.556
Commander Erwin!

19:00.931 --> 19:02.224
And the Military Police!

19:04.977 --> 19:07.146
I never thought
they'd ride along the wall.

19:07.896 --> 19:09.690
That's probably the quickest route.

19:11.692 --> 19:12.818
Krista...

19:13.944 --> 19:16.572
I'd prefer if you stayed back.

19:17.239 --> 19:19.825
No matter what you say, I won't.

19:20.075 --> 19:23.537
I refuse to wait here
when Ymir has been taken away.

19:24.204 --> 19:25.873
You two should know how I feel.

19:26.623 --> 19:28.625
Krista has a point, Armin.

19:29.918 --> 19:33.422
We have plenty of reasons
to go after them.

19:34.047 --> 19:35.841
Even if I can't believe one of them...

19:37.217 --> 19:39.511
That Reiner and Bertholdt are our enemies.

19:40.929 --> 19:43.265
I've got to hear it from their mouths.

19:47.895 --> 19:50.397
You made it, Commander Erwin!

19:51.231 --> 19:52.649
Is the situation here the same?

19:52.900 --> 19:53.901
Yes, sir!

19:53.984 --> 19:54.818
Good.

19:54.902 --> 19:56.361
Deploy the lifts!

19:58.113 --> 19:59.114
Hanji!

19:59.656 --> 20:00.741
Moblit...

20:01.325 --> 20:02.576
Give me a map.

20:07.915 --> 20:11.460
It might be a long shot,
but there's a giant forest here.

20:11.752 --> 20:13.086
We should head straight for it.

20:14.046 --> 20:18.008
It's not like they have a way
to hide the Armored Titan's footsteps,

20:19.051 --> 20:21.386
but I think that's where they're headed.

20:22.262 --> 20:23.138
Why is that?

20:24.014 --> 20:27.601
It's a gamble, but even if they have
the strength to change into Titans,

20:27.935 --> 20:31.355
the other Titans outside the wall
might still be a threat.

20:32.356 --> 20:34.107
Especially after all that fighting.

20:34.775 --> 20:38.946
They might not be as injured as Eren,
but I'm sure they're exhausted.

20:39.947 --> 20:41.615
Like how Annie was out cold for a while.

20:42.741 --> 20:47.204
Let's say for now that their destination
is somewhere outside of Wall Maria.

20:47.788 --> 20:50.374
Considering the distance
they'll have to cover,

20:50.540 --> 20:53.669
we can assume
they'll need to recover their stamina.

20:54.503 --> 20:59.299
Which means they'll want to rest somewhere
where Titans are unable to reach them.

21:00.300 --> 21:02.386
At least, until nightfall,
when Titans can't move.

21:28.036 --> 21:29.121
Oh, Eren.

21:35.460 --> 21:36.586
You're awake?

21:41.508 --> 21:42.718
We have until nightfall!

21:46.305 --> 21:50.809
If we reach the forest before nightfall,
we might still make it in time!

21:51.935 --> 21:53.020
Let's move!

23:32.285 --> 23:34.538
Eren wakes up and finds himself
in the giant forest.

23:35.622 --> 23:37.165
Desperate to escape,

23:37.499 --> 23:40.669
Eren tries to transform once again,
but is stopped by Ymir.

23:42.045 --> 23:43.839
Deep in the isolated forest,

23:44.422 --> 23:48.093
Eren and Reiner's emotions
clash violently.

23:49.261 --> 23:51.638
They must settle things once and for all.

23:52.305 --> 23:54.558
Not only for themselves,
but for all those who've died.

23:56.143 --> 23:59.187
Next episode, "Opening."
